# The script `mise run ffi-test` has two editors run against the config in
# `config/`, whose root imports `Greeting`, a module of the package
# `greeting`, which the config's `lakefile.toml` requires. It touches no
# file: the headless mode reads the lakefile and writes nothing.
#
# On the default set's editor, which does not link that package, what it
# prints must be exactly `expected`: the reload is rejected, and the
# diagnostic at the import names the package and says the package set needs
# a rebuild. On the fixture set's editor, which links it, what it prints
# must be exactly `installed-expected`: the config loads.
reload
settle

# The package's command, compiled into an editor whose set holds the
# package and into no other.
run greeting-hello
